{
 "encounter_id": "00622",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Um, hello. I think I might have broken my ankle? I came down the stairs wrong about an hour ago."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Oh dear, let's have a look at it in a second. Tell me what happened. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I missed the last two steps, I think, and I landed on the side of my foot. It sort of folded under me."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Did you hear or feel anything crack when it happened?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I felt something, a sort of pop. I'm not sure if I heard it. Is that bad?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It can mean different things, so don't read too much into it. Can you put weight on it at all?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Not really. I tried to hobble and it hurt too much. I'd say it's severe when I stand."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Where exactly is the pain?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Outside of the ankle, down towards the little toe side. And it's swollen, it's gone puffy already."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Anything else? Numbness, tingling, anything odd in the foot?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "My toes have been tingling a bit, but I can't say when that started. Maybe in the car, maybe before."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Okay, I'll test that properly in a moment. Any pain in your knee?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, my knee's fine. Foot's just a bit stiff."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Did you bang your head or hurt anywhere else when you fell?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, I only fell the last bit. Just the ankle."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Good. Have you hurt this ankle before?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A few years ago I twisted it playing netball, but nothing like this."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Okay. Let me check your pulse and so on first. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Pulse 84, blood pressure 124 over 76, temperature 36.7.",
   "pause": 10.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Is that all right? I feel a bit shaky. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Perfectly fine, the shakiness is just the shock. Now I'm going to press along the bone gently, and tell me when it hurts. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Ow, right there! ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "That's tender over the outer ankle bone and there's swelling around it. Your toes are warm and pink and you can feel me touching them.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "So is it broken? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It could be a fracture, or a bad sprain, and I can't tell which by looking. That's why I'd like an X-ray of the ankle now."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Oh. Right. How long will that take? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "We'll take you straight there. Meanwhile keep the foot raised on this stool."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Raised. Okay. Can I walk on it to the toilet? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Please don't put any weight through it at all. Ask a nurse for a wheelchair if you need to go."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No weight. Right. And what happens after the X-ray? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'll come and tell you what it shows, and we'll plan from there. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Thank you. Sorry, I'm very nervous. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Perfectly understandable. You've done the right thing coming in. ~"
  }
 ],
